{"name":"Black Mana","hex":"#858585","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"mana","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Power, prestige; specifically, a form of supernatural energy in Polynesian religion that inheres in things or people. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Magical energy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of mina (“ancient unit of weight or currency”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mana (series)","blocks":[{"text":"The Mana series, known in Japan as Seiken Densetsu , is an action role-playing game series created by Koichi Ishii, with development formerly from Square, and is currently owned by Square Enix. The series began in 1991 as Final Fantasy Adventure, a Game Boy handheld side story to Square's flagship franchise Final Fantasy. The Final Fantasy elements were subsequently dropped starting with the second installment, Secret of Mana, in order to become its own series. It has grown to include games of various genres within the fictional world of Mana, with recurring stories involving a world tree, its associated holy sword, and the fight against forces that would steal their power. Several character designs, creatures, and musical themes reappear frequently."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mana_(series)"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/72/Ringmenu.png/330px-Ringmenu.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/72/Ringmenu.png/330px-Ringmenu.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Mana series' Ring Command menu (from Trials of Mana)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARingmenu.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Mana_Tree.jpg/250px-Mana_Tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Mana_Tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Mana_Tree.jpg/250px-Mana_Tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artwork of the Mana Tree, from Children of Mana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMana_Tree.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/04/Rabite_Mana.png/250px-Rabite_Mana.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/04/Rabite_Mana.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/